## Build editions

- **`CHECKLISTDEK_BUILD`** — `full` (default in repo dev) or `community` (WordPress.org zip). Helpers in `includes/checklistdek-build.php`: `checklistdek_is_community_build()`, `checklistdek_includes_pro_package()`, `checklistdek_can_auto_deploy_client_panel()`, `checklistdek_get_licensing_file()`, `checklistdek_get_client_panel_layouts_file()`, `checklistdek_get_mu_plugin_installer_file()`, `checklistdek_get_mainwp_agent_file()`, `checklistdek_require_pro_modules()`, `checklistdek_get_webhook_dispatcher_file()`, `checklistdek_get_drift_cron_file()`.
- **Full build** loads Pro PHP (`class-checklistdek-auto-capture.php`, `class-checklistdek-email-notifier.php`, real webhook dispatcher + drift cron). After `checklistdek-build.php`, bootstrap requires `includes/checklistdek-freemius.php` when `!checklistdek_is_community_build()` — initializes Freemius via `cld_fs()` (`vendor/freemius/start.php`), fires `cld_fs_loaded`; SDK is org-compliant (`is_org_compliant`) so the WordPress.org zip stays separate. Premium purchase/licensing is Freemius-driven on full/premium zips — no hub Billing submenu, plan storage UI, or `/billing/*` REST in plugin code.
- **Community build** (`php bin/build-community-zip.php` → `dist/checklistdek-community.zip`): injects `define( 'CHECKLISTDEK_BUILD', 'community' );` in bootstrap; strips the Freemius `require_once` block; ships `includes/community/` stubs (`class-checklistdek-mu-plugin-installer.php`, `class-checklistdek-mainwp-agent.php`, `client-panel-layouts.php`, webhook/cron dispatchers); omits `includes/class-checklistdek-mu-plugin-installer.php`, `includes/integrations/class-checklistdek-mainwp-agent.php`, `includes/client-panel-layouts.php`, `mu-plugin/checklistdek-client/class-rest-api-install.php`, auto-capture, email notifier, full webhook/cron classes, `includes/checklistdek-freemius.php`, entire `vendor/`, and template JSON outside Community categories (`security`, `maintenance`, `performance`, `ecommerce`). All builds load `includes/community/class-checklistdek-licensing.php` via `checklistdek_get_licensing_file()` (build-edition gates only). Uses `register_uninstall_hook( …, CHECKLISTDEK_Uninstaller::run )` (no root `uninstall.php`). Community hub: three panel layouts in Settings (`checklistdek_get_client_panel_layouts_file()` → `includes/community/client-panel-layouts.php`); templates/categories limited by packaged JSON, not runtime plan filters. `checklistdek_can_auto_deploy_client_panel()` is false — manual mu-plugin upload + **Retry panel install** (probe only); no hub REST/local/MainWP file writes.
- **Pro / premium zip** (`php bin/build-pro-zip.php` → `dist/checklistdek-pro.zip`): ships full repo plugin tree (default `CHECKLISTDEK_BUILD` `full`), all template JSON, Pro PHP, `includes/checklistdek-freemius.php`, and `vendor/freemius/`; excludes dev-only paths (`.git`, `.cursor`, `bin/`, `includes/community/`, etc.). Uninstall cleanup runs via Freemius `after_uninstall` → `CHECKLISTDEK_Uninstaller::run()` (same option/table/cap cleanup as Community).
- Do not call Pro-only classes directly from shared code without `checklistdek_includes_pro_package()` or licensing gates — Community zips must not fatal on missing files.

## Terminology

Use **Checklist** in all user-facing copy, REST paths (`/checklists`), table names (`checklistdek_checklists`), PHP classes (`CHECKLISTDEK_Checklist_*`), and JS (`initChecklists`, `data-checklistdek-page="checklists"`). Legacy `workflow_*` identifiers exist only in DB migration and backward-compat audit/webhook reads — never in new code.

## Architecture

- Bootstrap defines constants, requires `checklistdek-build.php`, conditionally requires `checklistdek-freemius.php` (full build only), then core includes; conditionally loads Pro modules and webhook/cron class paths; registers activation/deactivation hooks; Community registers `register_uninstall_hook( …, CHECKLISTDEK_Uninstaller::run )`, full build hooks `cld_fs()->add_action( 'after_uninstall', … )` to the same uninstaller (no root `uninstall.php`); calls `checklistdek_run_plugin()`.
- `CHECKLISTDEK_Plugin::run()` wires admin UI, `CHECKLISTDEK_REST_API::register()`, `CHECKLISTDEK_Admin_Ajax::register()`, `CHECKLISTDEK_Drift_Cron::register()`.
- `CHECKLISTDEK_Plugin::init()` on `init`: `CHECKLISTDEK_Installer::maybe_install()`, `CHECKLISTDEK_Capabilities::register()`, `CHECKLISTDEK_Templates::bootstrap_builtin_templates()` (one-time `seed_builtin()`; `sync_builtin()` only when `CHECKLISTDEK_Plugin::should_sync_builtin_templates()` — admin, REST, cron, ajax — not public front-end), `CHECKLISTDEK_Licensing::sync_drift_cron()` (schedule or clear twicedaily drift cron based on build edition).
- Settings: `checklistdek_settings` via `CHECKLISTDEK_Settings` (group `checklistdek_settings_group`). Global kill switch: `enabled`. `exclude_options` blocks sensitive `/wp/v2/settings` fields from API checklist payloads on remote sites (`CHECKLISTDEK_Payload_Mapper::filter_excluded_payload()`). `client_panel_layout` (default `live_topbar`; catalog from `CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_layouts()` → `checklistdek_get_client_panel_layouts_file()` — nine layouts on full build, three on Community zip; sanitized via `CHECKLISTDEK_Licensing::sanitize_panel_layout()` / `get_effective_panel_layout()` for snapshots) controls how the client checklist panel renders on remote wp-admin; `client_panel_title` (default `Agency Checklist`, max 80 chars) sets the panel heading — both pushed in run snapshots via `CHECKLISTDEK_Client_Push::build_snapshot()`. `custom_site_groups` stores user-created site tag group slugs/labels (built-in groups: `general`, `client`, `project`, `tier`; reserved `integration`); catalog via `get_site_group_catalog()` / `add_custom_site_group()` and `GET|POST /sites/groups`. `wp_umbrella_api_token_enc` stores the encrypted WP Umbrella Public API token (Integrations connector modal — admin-ajax `checklistdek_save_wp_umbrella_token` with `normalize_wp_umbrella_api_token()` + `verify_api_token()` before save; sanitizer must preserve ciphertext when present, without `sanitize_text_field`). `CHECKLISTDEK_Settings::sanitize()` also explicitly preserves `onboarding_dismissed` and `custom_site_groups` for keys updated via REST/ajax, not the Settings form. Email alerts: `email_notification_events` (default `run_completed`; includes `run_cancelled`, `drift_detected`, etc.) + optional comma-separated `email_notification_address` (falls back to site admin email via `get_email_notification_addresses()`); independent from webhook `notification_events` (Settings form unchecked boxes → `[]`). Notifications: `CHECKLISTDEK_Webhook_Dispatcher::dispatch()` calls `CHECKLISTDEK_Email_Notifier::dispatch()` first (wp_mail when event enabled), then Slack/Discord/Teams only when the event is in `notification_events` and a channel URL is set.
- Custom tables via `CHECKLISTDEK_Installer` (`DB_VERSION` `1.7.0`, option `checklistdek_db_version`). All DB access through `*_Repository` classes. On every `maybe_install()`, `migrate_launchdek_branding()` idempotently renames legacy `launchdek_*` tables/options/caps to `checklistdek_*` (reads `launchdek_db_version` into `checklistdek_db_version` when needed). Upgrades from pre-1.1.0 rename `checklistdek_workflows` → `checklistdek_checklists`, `workflow_id` → `checklist_id`, and migrate legacy capability keys via `CHECKLISTDEK_Capabilities::migrate_workflow_caps()`. Upgrades to 1.2.0 add `checklistdek_sites.client_agent` and `checklistdek_runs.client_run_token`. Upgrades to 1.3.0 add `checklistdek_run_steps.notes_json` for per-step client evidence. Upgrades to 1.4.0 add `checklistdek_runs.is_archived` (soft-hide from site history; archive via `CHECKLISTDEK_Run_Repository::archive()`, permanent delete via `::delete()`). Upgrades to 1.5.0 add `checklistdek_sites.integration_source` and `checklistdek_sites.external_id` (indexed pair for connector site inventory sync). Upgrades to 1.6.0 add composite indexes for run history, run steps, audit site filters, and site tag filters (`migrate_performance_indexes()` via idempotent `add_index_if_missing()`). Version `1.7.0` marks the ChecklistDek rebrand (no new columns beyond branding migration).
- Remote calls: `CHECKLISTDEK_Remote_Client` (Application Password basic auth) — never store plaintext passwords outside vault. `request()` tries pretty `/wp-json/` first, then `?rest_route=` when the response is `rest_no_route` (broken rewrites on local/MAMP installs). Transport and remote error text passes through `sanitize_remote_message()` (`wp_strip_all_tags` + `sanitize_textarea_field`) before `last_error` storage and REST/admin display.
- Checklist engine: `CHECKLISTDEK_Checklist_Runner::start()` creates run → `execute_next()` / `auto_advance()` / `execute_all_auto()` → `CHECKLISTDEK_Step_Executor` → `CHECKLISTDEK_Payload_Mapper` for `api` steps; `manual` steps set `awaiting_manual` until `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete` (revert via `/uncomplete` → `CHECKLISTDEK_Step_Executor::mark_manual_incomplete()`). Run/step/client events trigger `CHECKLISTDEK_Webhook_Dispatcher::dispatch()` (email when event is in `email_notification_events`; Slack/Discord/Teams only when the same event is in `notification_events` and a channel URL is set). Drift: after each verify, `CHECKLISTDEK_Drift_Verifier::maybe_dispatch_drift_notification()` dispatches `drift_detected` only for configuration checks newly in `drift` status vs the previous stored snapshot—not on every recurring cron pass. Step admin paths resolve via `CHECKLISTDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::resolve_path()` — priority: explicit `deep_link` (`normalize_stored_path()`), API route/payload inference (`path_from_api_step()` for `/wp/v2/settings` and common core REST routes), then title/instructions keyword inference (`infer_path_from_text()`). On checklist save, `CHECKLISTDEK_Checklist_Repository` stores `deep_link` as a normalized admin path (not `esc_url_raw()`). Hub run tracker and client snapshots use `CHECKLISTDEK_Remote_Client::admin_link()` for full URLs; snapshots also include `admin_path` so the client panel can rebuild local `admin_url()` links. `CHECKLISTDEK_Templates::repair_builtin_deep_links()` (once via `checklistdek_deep_links_repaired`) restores paths stripped by legacy URL sanitization.
- Client checklist panel: when `checklistdek_can_auto_deploy_client_panel()` (full/Pro hub), `CHECKLISTDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::ensure_installed()` deploys the bundled `mu-plugin/` via remote REST (`POST /client/install` from `CHECKLISTDEK_Client_REST_API_Install`), local same-server path inference (`get_hub_document_root()`), or MainWP ZIP push; runs on site save/test with credentials and when `push_run()` uses `$sync_bundle = true`. Community hub uses the stub installer — probe-only `ensure_installed()` (no file writes); manual bootstrap via **Download checklistdek-client.php** (`GET /panel/bootstrap`) and upload to `wp-content/mu-plugins/`, then **Retry panel install** (`POST /sites/{id}/panel/install` verifies presence). When the panel is missing, connection test/save responses include `client_panel` `{ success, message }`; admin UI shows shared **Client checklist panel setup** block (`checklistdek-panel-setup-block.php`) on Sites editor modal, connection tester, and onboarding step 2 (tester block omits retry until site is saved). `push_run( $run_id, $prepare = true, $sync_bundle = null )` — `$sync_bundle` defaults to `$prepare`; auto-advances API steps when `$prepare` is true; pushes a run snapshot to the remote panel (`POST /checklistdek/v1/client/run`); uses `CHECKLISTDEK_Run_Repository::ensure_client_token()` for per-run `client_run_token` callbacks (backfills legacy runs). `sync_run()` calls `push_run( $run_id, false, false )` — snapshot-only re-push with no step advancement and no bundle reinstall. Hub run handlers call `sync_run()` after hub-side step advances. Client token callbacks (`/client-runs/...`) pass `$skip_client_sync = true` — hub returns `snapshot` in the response instead of re-pushing; client panel applies it locally (optimistic UI with rollback on error). Client manual completions/uncompletions hit hub `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete|uncomplete` with `X-ChecklistDek-Run-Token`. Client notes save locally first on the remote site, then sync to hub; hub snapshots merge notes via `filter_step_notes()` / `merge_step_notes()` rather than wiping local entries. Sites REST responses expose `client_agent` when the panel is detected.
- Admin UI: thin partials in `admin/partials/` with `data-checklistdek-page`; JS drives CRUD via REST (`checklistdekAdmin` global) with admin-ajax for integration actions and site run history (`CHECKLISTDEK_Admin_Ajax`). Checklists use a three-column builder — vertical drag-and-drop canvas, step config sidebar (client panel heading field `#checklistdek-cl-panel-title` auto-saves via `POST /settings/client-panel-title`; multicheck role mapping dropdown; live deep-link inference via `POST /checklists/infer-deep-link`; per-step `show_note_field` / `show_screenshot_field` toggles; Step Type + API Payload Mapper field tooltips), and live client-panel preview (`#checklistdek-checklist-preview` via `renderChecklistPreview()` — mirrors sidebar layout using bundled `mu-plugin/checklistdek-client/css/checklistdek-client-admin.css` enqueued on the Checklists screen only).
- Dashboard cache: `CHECKLISTDEK_Dashboard_Cache` stores stats (including lean `CHECKLISTDEK_Run_Repository::completion_rate()` aggregate), connection health counts, the 15-entry live log feed (`CHECKLISTDEK_Audit_Log::get_feed()` with `include_details => false`), filtered sites list payloads (`get_sites_list()` / `refresh_sites_list()` — delegates to `CHECKLISTDEK_Site_Repository::all()` with batched tags and list-only credential flags), and quick-launch picker options (`quick_launch`: lightweight `sites` + `checklists` id/title pairs via `picker_list()`, cap `PICKER_LIMIT` 500 each) in `checklistdek_dashboard_cache` (non-autoload). Feed entries include `show_site_label` (from `CHECKLISTDEK_Audit_Log::feed_entry_show_site_label()`) so site-scoped actions render a separate site badge instead of embedding the site name in the message text. Repositories call `invalidate_stats()` / `invalidate_connections()` / `invalidate_sites_list()` / `invalidate_quick_launch_picker()` on site/checklist mutations; `CHECKLISTDEK_Audit_Log::log()` calls `invalidate_feed()`. Dashboard PHP partial and `checklistdekAdmin.dashboard` localize preloaded stats, connections, feed, and `quickLaunch` on first paint; Quick Launch Bar selects render server-side with `data-checklistdek-preloaded="1"` (JS skips REST fetch when preloaded). REST `/dashboard/*` and `/logs/feed` (default) read from cache.
- Activity logs: dedicated hidden submenu page (`PAGE_SLUG . '-activity-logs'`, registered then `remove_submenu_page`) reachable from Sites toolbar, per-site row **Activity Log** link (`?site_id=`), dashboard feed link, and legacy `?page={slug}-sites&activity_logs` redirect. Full filtered audit table via admin-ajax `checklistdek_get_activity_logs` (`verify_dashboard_request` / `VIEW_DASHBOARD`; delegates to `CHECKLISTDEK_Audit_Log::query()` + `list_query_args_from_input()`) with paginated shape `{ logs, has_more, offset, limit }`; REST `GET /logs/feed?detailed=1` (`can_view_dashboard`) uses the same arg builder for programmatic/Batch Run access. Supports `site_id` (matches direct `site_id` or run-linked entries via `EXISTS` on `checklistdek_runs`), `status`, `date_from`, `date_to`, `search`, `limit` (default `LIST_DEFAULT_LIMIT` 50, max `LIST_MAX_LIMIT` 100), `offset`, and `include_details` (default false — lean list rows). First page preloaded in PHP as `checklistdekAdmin.activityLogs.initialFeed` when default filters match (`initialSiteId` from `?site_id=`). `CHECKLISTDEK_Audit_Log::find()` + batch user/site/run/step lookups in `build_query_context()` / `format_row()`; formatted rows expose `details_summary`, `detail_fields` (`format_activity_detail_fields()`), contextual `action_label`, `outcome_class`, `has_details`, and legacy `detail_lines` / `show_run_timeline`. Activity Logs **What happened** shows summary teaser + **View details** (labeled fields) and nested **View raw data** (`GET /logs/{id}?details_only=1` → `get_decoded_details()`; JS cache + prefetch on **View details** expand). When a site filter is active, JS hides the Site column (`.checklistdek-audit-table--hide-site-col`). Batch Run Run tab keeps compact feed copy with optional **View raw data**. Activity Logs page preloads site filter via `checklistdekAdmin.activityLogs.sites` (`CHECKLISTDEK_Site_Repository::picker_list()`). Batch Run Run tab shows a compact site-scoped recent activity feed (`#checklistdek-run-activity-feed`, limit 8) instead of a duplicate full audit table.
- Sites page run history: each site row has a chevron toggle (`.checklistdek-site-history-toggle`) that expands a nested runs panel (`.checklistdek-site-runs-row` → `.checklistdek-site-runs-panel`); loads via admin-ajax `checklistdek_get_site_runs` on first expand (delegates to `CHECKLISTDEK_Run_Repository::list_for_site_history()` — lean JOIN + batched step progress; default `limit` 25, optional `offset`, returns `{ runs, has_more, offset, limit }`; cached in JS with in-flight deduplication and **Load more** pagination). REST `GET /sites/{id}/runs` remains registered for programmatic access. Table columns: Checklist, Steps (fraction + status badge + progress bar), Started, **Completed** (— when in progress), By — no **View run** column (open runs from Batch Run or dashboard). Name column shows full site name + URL (`.checklistdek-site-name-cell`, `.checklistdek-site-url-link`) and optional **Client panel** badge. **Add to group** modal (`#checklistdek-add-to-group-modal`) and site editor tag group select (`#checklistdek-site-group`) use preloaded `checklistdekAdmin.sites.groups` / `GET /sites/groups`; inline **Add group…** step posts `POST /sites/groups` `{ label }`. Site row Actions dropdown: Push Checklist, Test, **Add to group**, **More info** (site details modal `#checklistdek-site-info-modal`), **Activity Log**, Delete. Site row Actions use Edit + dropdown; combined Connection + Health badge in Status column.
- Dashboard onboarding: one-time post-activation redirect via option `CHECKLISTDEK_Admin::ACTIVATION_REDIRECT_OPTION` (`checklistdek_activation_redirect` — activating user ID, or `1` when unknown); `CHECKLISTDEK_Admin::maybe_activation_redirect()` runs on `admin_init` for users with `VIEW_DASHBOARD`, skips ajax/network admin/bulk activate, matches stored user when ID > 1, clears the flag only after eligibility checks pass (so unrelated admin requests do not consume it), honors legacy transient when option is empty, skips redirect when already on the dashboard page, then `wp_safe_redirect` to `?onboarding=1`. Admin navigation reads `$_GET` via `get_admin_query_page()` / `get_admin_query_absint()` / `has_admin_query_flag()`. Deactivation and uninstall clear the option (and legacy transient). Opens a 2-step modal — **Step 1**: paste plain-text SOPs with placeholder-as-sample live preview, or **Start from a template** via the shared template picker (`importMode: populate` loads steps into paste/preview); **Step 2**: optional existing-site picker (`#checklistdek-onboarding-existing-sites` — hidden until `GET /sites` returns at least one site) or new-site connect/test (App Passwords) → `#checklistdek-onboarding-panel-setup` when panel missing after test/save → create checklist + site + optional first run (`POST /runs`). Segmented progress UI with labeled step hints. Dismissal persisted via `onboarding_dismissed` (`POST /onboarding/dismiss`, `can_view_dashboard`); Settings can re-show via `POST /onboarding/reset` (`can_manage_settings`) + **Show onboarding wizard** button. Modal markup in `checklistdek-onboarding-modal.php` (required on dashboard + settings); logic in `initOnboarding()` (global init, not dashboard-only). Auto-opens only on the dashboard screen when `onboarding.show` is true (not on Settings after save); `?onboarding=1` still opens on any page with the modal. Exposes `window.checklistdekOpenOnboarding`.
- Template picker: shared modal (`checklistdek-template-picker-modal.php`) with capsule category filters, selectable template list, steps preview panel, **Start blank instead**, and **Import Template**. Included on dashboard, checklists, and settings. Checklists **New Checklist** tab **Start from Template** opens picker → default `importMode: checklist` via `POST /templates/{slug}/clone` → `onImport(checklist)` opens **My Checklists** builder; onboarding uses `importMode: populate` to fill paste text. Logic in `initTemplatePicker()` (global init); exposes `window.checklistdekOpenTemplatePicker(callbacks)`.
- Checklists page sections: unified `nav-tab-wrapper` (`.checklistdek-checklist-nav`) with three tabs — **Templates** (default — built-in category grid with `#checklistdek-builtin-template-search` cross-category search by title/description/slug/step text, agency vault with info tooltip), **My Checklists** (dropdown picker `#checklistdek-checklist-select`, three-column builder + **Start Blank** + import/export), and **Auto-Capture** (inline panel, not a modal). Tab panels use `[data-checklistdek-tab-panel]` (`templates|my-checklists|auto-capture`); tab state via `?tab=` (`templates` clears param) or `?checklist_id={id}` (opens **My Checklists**; legacy `?tab=builder` normalizes to `my-checklists`; legacy `?tab=new-checklist` normalizes to `templates`). Template/built-in and vault cards use **Use Checklist** (`createChecklistFromTemplate()` → `openChecklistEditor()`). Custom checklists are selected only via the **My Checklists** dropdown (no custom checklist card grid on Templates). Legacy `?page={slug}-templates` redirects to Checklists (`maybe_redirect_legacy_templates_page()`).
- Custom checklist list performance: `CHECKLISTDEK_Checklist_Repository::summary_list()` returns lightweight rows (`id`, `title`, `description`, `steps_count`, step id/title preview); `GET /checklists?summary=1` (optional `is_template`, `is_vault`); full `GET /checklists` list defaults to `LIST_DEFAULT_LIMIT` 500 (max `LIST_MAX_LIMIT` 1000); `GET /templates/vault` uses the same summary shape. Checklists screen preloads non-template summaries in `checklistdekAdmin.customChecklists`; admin JS deduplicates via `fetchCustomChecklistSummaries()` / `refreshCustomChecklistUi()` (one request for picker + vault select).
- Sites list performance: `CHECKLISTDEK_Site_Repository::all()` uses lean `list_select_columns()` (excludes credential blob), `format_list()` with batched `get_tags_map()`, and `row_has_stored_credentials()` / `has_credentials_flag` so list screens avoid vault decrypt; `GET /sites` and Sites admin preload read `CHECKLISTDEK_Dashboard_Cache::get_sites_list()` (filtered cache keys in `sites_lists`).
- Auto-capture: user-initiated recording on a connected client site with the checklist panel installed. Hub `CHECKLISTDEK_Auto_Capture` proxies to remote `GET|POST|DELETE /checklistdek/v1/client/capture`; client `CHECKLISTDEK_Client_Auto_Capture` hooks admin actions (REST settings, plugin toggles) into manual/api steps stored in `checklistdek_client_capture` option. Checklists **Auto-Capture** tab panel (`#checklistdek-panel-auto-capture`, `.checklistdek-auto-capture-panel`) uses hub `/sites/{id}/capture` routes; **Import Captured Steps** loads steps into the builder and switches to **My Checklists**.
- Batch Run page (menu label **Batch Run**, slug `-automation`): nav tabs **Run Checklist** / **Batch Queue** / **Drift Monitor** (`.checklistdek-automation-nav`, `[data-checklistdek-automation-tab]` / `[data-checklistdek-automation-panel]`). Run tab uses a 3-step wizard inside `.checklistdek-automation-wizard` (`#checklistdek-automation-progress`, steps 1–3: choose checklist → single target site → execute) with full-width step runner and progress bar; **Recent Activity** card (`.checklistdek-automation-run-activity`) shows site-scoped feed when a run is active; batch tab has separate `#checklistdek-batch-checklist` / `#checklistdek-batch-site-picker` pickers and queue table; drift tab hosts verifier controls with user-friendly copy. Full Activity Logs page is separate (hidden submenu).
- Remote architecture: targets need WP 6.2+ with Application Passwords enabled. Core API checklist steps use only core REST. The client admin panel is a lightweight mu-plugin bundle (Pro hub may auto-deploy when credentials allow; WordPress.org Community hub requires manual upload; **Retry panel install** verifies) — not a separate wordpress.org download.

## Licensing & build edition (`CHECKLISTDEK_Licensing`)

- **Single licensing class** — all builds load `includes/community/class-checklistdek-licensing.php` via `checklistdek_get_licensing_file()`. Gates Pro PHP/UI with `checklistdek_includes_pro_package()` (`CHECKLISTDEK_BUILD` full vs community), not hub plan tiers. `OPTION_NAME` (`checklistdek_billing`) is legacy — removed on uninstall/migration only; no `get_plan()`, `set_plan()`, Billing UI, or `/billing/*` REST. Premium distribution uses Freemius (`includes/checklistdek-freemius.php`, `cld_fs()`).
- **Community** (WordPress.org zip): unlimited connected sites (`can_add_site()` always true); built-in templates limited by **packaged** JSON at zip build time (four categories); **three** client panel layouts in Settings (`live_topbar`, `bottom_dock`, `floating_pill`); no hub auto-deploy of client panel files, Private Agency Vault, auto-capture, email/webhook notifications (`CHECKLISTDEK_Webhook_Dispatcher` / Settings save skip when `!can_use_notifications()`), MainWP **Push Client Panel** install, or scheduled drift cron (manual drift verify on Batch Run still available). Pro-only admin tabs/sections omitted via `checklistdek_includes_pro_package()` in partials (not disabled upgrade UI).
- **Full / Pro zip**: all **86** template JSON files and **nine** panel layouts (`includes/client-panel-layouts.php`); hub auto-deploy + MainWP panel push; vault, auto-capture, notifications, scheduled drift; Freemius SDK bundled.
- Pro-only REST routes register only when `checklistdek_includes_pro_package()` (e.g. `/sites/{id}/capture`, `/templates/vault`) — absent on Community builds, not `checklistdek_pro_required` responses. `/templates` catalog reflects templates present in the install (`filter_builtin_templates()` passthrough; `get_template_categories_for_plan()` derives category metadata from the shipped catalog).
- **Admin JS** (all plugin screens): omit capture/vault-related `strings.*` when `!can_use_auto_capture()` / `!can_use_agency_vault()`. No `checklistdekAdmin.billing` or billing gate strings. Hub and client admin scripts depend on `heartbeat` and refresh the `wp_rest` nonce on bare jQuery `heartbeat-tick` (`rest_nonce` — not namespaced handlers). Community UI: Settings omits **Webhooks & Email** tab and scheduled-drift toggle; Checklists omits Auto-Capture tab and vault section (PHP)—no disabled Pro controls or upgrade notices in those screens. `CHECKLISTDEK_Admin_Ajax` registers the same handlers on Community and Pro (capability-gated, not package-gated).
- **Drift cron**: `CHECKLISTDEK_Licensing::sync_drift_cron()` on activation and every `init` — calls `CHECKLISTDEK_Drift_Cron::activate()` only when `can_use_scheduled_drift()`; otherwise `::deactivate()`. Cron `run()` no-ops when the build lacks scheduled drift.

